# Who is asked to review what.
#
# `main` requires one approval, and rules/security.md requires a SECOND reviewer for the four
# areas below. This file is what turns that rule into a request GitHub sends, instead of
# something a reviewer has to remember. Ownership here is about who must look, not about who
# may change: anyone may open the pull request.

# Everything, by default.
*                                   @edgar2031

# Authentication, sessions and tokens. A mistake here is not a bug that shows up as an
# exception — it is a caller silently treated as somebody else.
